<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: PRAGUE BREWER POSTS 96 NET LOSS.</title>
<headline>PRAGUE BREWER POSTS 96 NET LOSS.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Czech brewer Prazske Pivovary a.s., majority-owned by British brewing group Bass Plc, on Monday said it posted a net loss for 1996 of 119.1 million crowns, calculated according to international accounting standards (IAS).</p>
<p>Comparative figures were not immediately available.</p>
</text>
